BT /F2 7.8 Tf 0.12 0.31 0.58 rg 58.0 640.0 Td (EMPIRICAL BENCHMARKS ON AI RESEARCH ENGINE RELIABILITY:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 0.25 0.30 0.35 rg 58.0 629.0 Td (- Columbia University Tow Center (2025): 1,600 queries across 8 AI search engines returned incorrect answers >60% of the time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.3 Tf 0.25 0.30 0.35 rg 58.0 619.0 Td (- BBC & EBU Investigation: 3,000+ AI answers audited; nearly 50% had significant errors, 1 in 5 had severe factual inaccuracies.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.10 0.15 0.25 rg 48.0 598.0 Td (The Six Ways AI Citations Fail in Practice:) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg 48.0 586.0 Td (- 1. Nonexistent Source:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.30 0.30 0.30 rg 58.0 575.5 Td (  Hallucinated URLs, fabricated authors, or dead DOIs that sound plausible but never existed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg 48.0 563.5 Td (- 2. Metadata Mismatch:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.30 0.30 0.30 rg 58.0 553.0 Td (  The cited article is real, but publication year, authors, or sponsoring institutions are scrambled.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg 48.0 541.0 Td (- 3. Unsubstantiated Claim:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.30 0.30 0.30 rg 58.0 530.5 Td (  The source exists, but nowhere in its body does it make or validate the statement the model attributed to it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg 48.0 518.5 Td (- 4. Overstated Support:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.30 0.30 0.30 rg 58.0 508.0 Td (  The research paper claims modest laboratory correlation; the LLM asserts universal, definitive causation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg 48.0 496.0 Td (- 5. Outdated Context:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.30 0.30 0.30 rg 58.0 485.5 Td (  Factually accurate when written, but rendered obsolete by newer regulatory rulings or market events.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 0.15 0.20 0.30 rg 48.0 473.5 Td (- 6. Circular Loops:) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.8 Tf 0.30 0.30 0.30 rg 58.0 463.0 Td (  Secondary aggregator blogs circularly quoting AI summaries without any underlying empirical proof.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 0.10 0.15 0.25 rg 48.0 445.0 Td (4. Reading for Load-Bearing Claims & Claim Atomization) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.25 rg 48.0 431.0 Td (A load-bearing claim is an assertion that carries the weight of a document's core thesis. If that single claim is disproven,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.25 rg 48.0 420.2 Td (the entire strategic recommendation collapses. Writers must distinguish between three distinct layers: Factual Claims \(what) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.25 rg 48.0 409.4 Td (happened\), Interpretations \(what the author believes it means\), and Recommendations \(what action they advocate\).) Tj ET
